title: EMR Connect › No connection › Import a record and start a New Case
route: /emr
intro: For a record system that has no connection: one small row under Connection health opens the shared import in a side panel. Import an export (CSV or XLSX with field mapping, or a PDF) or paste a screenshot; on Apply, a New Case starts with the patient filled in.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the screenshot reading and the PDF reading are simulated and say so. Files and images stay in the browser.
---
start s1 "Open EMR Connect"
screen sc "Row under Connection health\n'No connection for a system? Import an export or paste a screenshot'\nButton 'Import a record'"
click c1 "Click 'Import a record'"
overlay o1 "Side panel 'Import a record'\n'Import a file' and 'Paste a screenshot'\nNo 'Pull from EMR' here"
click cFile "Click 'Import a file'"
click cShot "Click 'Paste a screenshot', or press Ctrl+V or Cmd+V in the panel"
goto gFile "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Import › Import a file with field mapping"
goto gShot "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Import › Paste a screenshot"
screen sRev "Review: '9 fields found', a box for each\n'Apply 10'"
click cApply "Click 'Apply 10'"
store st1 "A new case is made at the site in view\nThe patient, coverage and request are filled; the notes become documents"
toast t1 "'Applied 9 fields and 1 document'"
process p1 "New Case opens on Intake with the case\nEach filled field says 'From file' or 'From screenshot'"
goto gIntake "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Intake › Initial authorization"
click cEsc "Press Escape, click outside, or the X"
endx e1 "Panel closes; nothing is made"

s1 --> sc --> c1 --> o1
o1 --> cFile --> gFile
o1 --> cShot --> gShot
gFile -.-> sRev
gShot -.-> sRev
sRev --> cApply --> st1 --> t1 --> p1 --> gIntake
o1 --> cEsc --> e1
